  "method": "Known independent detector variance propagated through the squared composite Gaussian sigma 1, discrete Laplacian, and Bayer green interpolation impulse response. Evaluate interior only; 128 varying-variance noise draws per colour mode. Four seeds for each mono/RGGB spatial-blur, uniform-blur and flat case at noise sigma 4/12; independent 16-frame template and 48 stack frames. Correction subtracts expected noise energy before clipping and local normalization, preserving the same scalar global weight and correlation gate. All frames retained; no sharpening.",
  "caveat": "These quality maps use the native green proxy. The production preprocessing quality score instead uses a 2x2 area-mean luminance plane; its estimator and screening are not changed or assessed by this experiment.",
  "decision": "Noise propagation agrees with Monte Carlo within 0.4%. Known-noise correction improves the spatial-blur controls, with no meaningful harm on uniform/flat controls. Automatic same-colour second-difference MAD noise estimates confuse sharp Bayer texture with noise, overestimating sigma up to 2.5 times. Do not adopt automatic subtraction; next perform bounded real-image sensitivity before investing in a calibrated estimator.",
